  <item id="ann-001">
    <title>Community Hall Reopening — Bookings Now Open</title>
    <summary>The Northside Community Hall has completed its renovation and is now accepting bookings for events, meetings, and functions.</summary>
    <content>
      We are pleased to announce that the Northside Community Hall renovation has been completed ahead of schedule.
      The hall has been upgraded with new accessible entrances, a modern kitchen, improved lighting, and a new PA system.
      Bookings are now open for community groups, private events, and council meetings.
      To book the hall, please visit the Services page or contact our events team directly.
    </content>
    <priority>high</priority>
    <status>published</status>
    <date>2026-03-10</date>
    <category>Facilities</category>
    <audience>all</audience>
    <author>CityLink Events Team</author>
  </item>

  <item id="ann-002">
    <title>Rates Notices — March Quarter Now Available Online</title>
    <summary>The March quarter rates notices have been issued. Residents can now view and pay their rates online through the portal.</summary>
    <content>
      March quarter rates notices have been issued to all ratepayers. You can now view your notice and make payment online through the portal.
      Payment options include credit/debit card, BPAY, and direct debit. The due date for this quarter is 31 March 2026.
      If you believe there is an error in your assessment, please contact the Rates team within 30 days of the notice date.
      Pensioner concessions and payment plans are available — contact us for more information.
    </content>
    <priority>high</priority>
    <status>published</status>
    <date>2026-03-05</date>
    <category>Finance</category>
    <audience>residents</audience>
    <author>CityLink Finance Department</author>
  </item>

  <item id="ann-003">
    <title>Free Community BBQ — Saturday 22 March</title>
    <summary>Join us for a free community BBQ at Riverside Park this Saturday. All welcome — bring the family!</summary>
    <content>
      CityLink Initiatives is hosting a free community BBQ at Riverside Park on Saturday 22 March 2026 from 11:00 AM to 2:00 PM.
      This is a great opportunity to meet your neighbours, find out about local services, and speak with council representatives.
      There will be free sausage sizzle, soft drinks, activities for kids, and live acoustic music.
      No registration required — just turn up! The event will be held rain or shine (undercover area available).
    </content>
    <priority>medium</priority>
    <status>published</status>
    <date>2026-03-14</date>
    <category>Community Events</category>
    <audience>all</audience>
    <author>CityLink Community Team</author>
  </item>

  <item id="ann-004">
    <title>Waste Collection Schedule Change — Easter Long Weekend</title>
    <summary>Kerbside waste and recycling collection will be one day later than usual during the Easter long weekend (18–21 April 2026).</summary>
    <content>
      Please note that due to the Easter public holidays, kerbside waste and recycling collections will be delayed by one day for the week of 18–21 April 2026.
      If your normal collection day is Friday 18 April (Good Friday), your bin will be collected on Saturday 19 April instead.
      All other collection days in that week will also shift forward by one day.
      Please ensure bins are placed at the kerbside by 6:00 AM on your revised collection day.
      The normal schedule resumes from Monday 28 April.
    </content>
    <priority>medium</priority>
    <status>published</status>
    <date>2026-03-01</date>
    <category>Waste Management</category>
    <audience>residents</audience>
    <author>CityLink Waste Services</author>
  </item>

  <item id="ann-005">
    <title>Portal Maintenance — Scheduled Downtime Sunday 23 March (2–4 AM)</title>
    <summary>The CityLink portal will be briefly offline for scheduled maintenance on Sunday 23 March between 2:00 AM and 4:00 AM AWST.</summary>
    <content>
      To continue improving the portal experience, we will be performing scheduled maintenance on Sunday 23 March 2026 between 2:00 AM and 4:00 AM AWST.
      During this window, the portal will be unavailable. This includes the events booking system, feedback submission, and account login.
      Emergency contact information will remain available on the homepage during the maintenance window.
      We apologise for any inconvenience. If you need to complete a time-sensitive task, please do so before 2:00 AM Sunday.
    </content>
    <priority>low</priority>
    <status>published</status>
    <date>2026-03-18</date>
    <category>System</category>
    <audience>all</audience>
    <author>CityLink IT Team</author>
  </item>

